## Global Rules

### DO

- Use design system atoms/molecules/organisms before creating custom elements.
- Use token mappings (`design-system/mappings/`) for colors, font sizes, shadows, z-index.
- Use `intl.formatMessage({ defaultMessage: '...' })` for all hardcoded UI strings.
- Use `cn()` from `classnames` for composing Tailwind class strings.
- Follow OxFmt: single quotes, no semicolons, 2-space indent.
- Mark client components with `'use client'` at the top.
- Use `findTldByLocale(locale)` + `notFound()` guard in every page.
- Use `useFactorialContext()` in client components for locale/host data.

### DON'T

- Don't install new dependencies — check `package.json` first.
- Don't import from `@factorialco/f0-react` — unused here.
- Don't hardcode color values (hex/rgb) — use token-based Tailwind classes.
- Don't create `.css` / `.module.css` files (rare exception: SCSS pseudo-elements).
- Don't use `i18n.t()` or `<FormattedMessage>` — use `intl.formatMessage()`.
- Don't use ESLint or Prettier — this project uses OxLint and OxFmt.

---

## Validation (All Webpage Work)

- No hardcoded color values, pixel spacing, or inline styles.
- Design system components reused where possible.
- `'use client'` only on components that need browser APIs or interactivity.
- `pnpm lint` from `webpage/` directory.
- `pnpm format <changed-files>` from `webpage/` directory.
- `pnpm test` for any touched test files.

